IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `eoa-dates`

-- Equal Opportunity Act 2010 (Vic) -- the rules, seat-neutral where the text is.
--
-- Parts 2 and 3 (what discrimination is; the positive duty), Part 4 Divisions 1 and 2 (employment and the
-- employment-related areas) with their exceptions, the Part 5 general exceptions an employer can rely on, Part 6 (sexual
-- harassment, every area), Part 7 (victimisation, authorising or assisting, discriminatory requests for information,
-- vicarious liability), Part 8 (dispute resolution by the Commission and applications to VCAT), and s 127 (when the
-- Commission may investigate). The questions of the person in the seat are in eoa-seat.l4.
--
-- Answers: JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE where the text answers; NOTHING where it does not, with a NOTHING-kind tag
-- (*limited by its own wording*, *silent*, *points outside the text*). See "Rulings on negatives" in NOTES.md.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Word file of the Equal
-- Opportunity Act 2010, Version No. 032 (15 April 2026), not the authorised version. (c) State of Victoria; published with
-- the authority of the Government Printer for the State of Victoria. No part may be reproduced except in accordance with
-- the Copyright Act 1968 (Cth). Quoted under the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Equal Opportunity Act 2010 -- the rules`

§§ `Helpers`

-- Either of two answers: yes if either is yes, no if both are no, otherwise not answered.
GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, b IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`either answer of` a `and` b MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN JUST x THEN
        IF x
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE b
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        CONSIDER b
        WHEN JUST y THEN
            IF y
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE NOTHING
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- The answer is yes.
GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the answer` a `is yes` IF
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN JUST x THEN x
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

-- The answer is no.
GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the answer` a `is no` IF
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN JUST x THEN (NOT x)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

§§ `Part 2 -- what is discrimination (ss 6 to 12)`

-- s 6: "The following are the attributes on the basis of which discrimination is prohibited in the areas of activity set
-- out in Part 4". s 4: "attribute means an attribute in section 6" (a "means" definition: anything else is not one).
DECLARE `Attribute` IS ONE OF
    `age`
    `breastfeeding`                          -- includes expressing milk (s 4)
    `employment activity`                    -- asking about, or raising a concern about, employment entitlements (s 4)
    `gender identity`
    `disability`                             -- s 4: loss of function, disease organisms, malfunction, disfigurement; includes a future disability and behaviour that is a symptom of one
    `industrial activity`                    -- union membership or activity, or not (s 4)
    `lawful sexual activity`
    `marital status`
    `parental status or status as a carer`
    `physical features`                      -- height, weight, size or other bodily characteristics (s 4)
    `political belief or activity`
    `pregnancy`
    `profession trade or occupation`
    `race`                                   -- includes colour, descent, nationality, ethnicity (s 4)
    `religious belief or activity`
    `sex`
    `sex characteristics`
    `sexual orientation`
    `an expunged homosexual conviction`
    `a spent conviction`
    `personal association with a person who has one of these attributes`
    `none of these attributes`

-- s 7(2): "Discrimination on the basis of an attribute includes discrimination on the basis -- (a) that a person has that
-- attribute or had it at any time ...; (b) of a characteristic that a person with that attribute generally has; (c) of a
-- characteristic that is generally imputed to a person with that attribute; (d) that a person is presumed to have that
-- attribute or to have had it at any time." (3): being accompanied by or possessing an assistance aid (equipment, a
-- helper such as an interpreter or reader, an assistance dog) is a characteristic a person with a disability generally has.
DECLARE `Basis of the treatment` IS ONE OF
    `an attribute I have now`
    `an attribute I had in the past`
    `a characteristic that people with the attribute generally have`
    `a characteristic generally imputed to people with the attribute`
    `an attribute I am presumed to have or to have had`
    `my assistance aid, helper or assistance dog`
    `something else`

-- s 4 "attribute means" (JUST FALSE for none); s 7(2) "includes" (NOTHING for something else: *the list is not closed*).
GIVEN `the attribute` IS AN `Attribute`, `the basis` IS A `Basis of the treatment`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(2), (3) -- the treatment was on the basis of an attribute` `the attribute` `the basis` MEANS
    IF `the attribute` EQUALS `none of these attributes`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE CONSIDER `the basis`
         WHEN `my assistance aid, helper or assistance dog` THEN
            IF `the attribute` EQUALS `disability`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE NOTHING
         WHEN `something else` THEN NOTHING
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- What happened, as the person can state it.
DECLARE `What happened` HAS
    `the attribute concerned`                   IS AN `Attribute`
    `the basis of what was done`                IS A `Basis of the treatment`
    `I was treated unfavourably`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the attribute was a substantial reason`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `a requirement was imposed`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the requirement disadvantages people with the attribute` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the requirement was proved reasonable`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was proved to be a special measure`     IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 8(1): "Direct discrimination occurs if a person treats, or proposes to treat, a person with an attribute unfavourably
-- because of that attribute." (2): awareness irrelevant; the attribute need not be the only or dominant reason, "provided
-- that it is a substantial reason". s 10: motive irrelevant.
GIVEN h IS A `What happened`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8 -- direct discrimination` h MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 7(2), (3) -- the treatment was on the basis of an attribute` (h's `the attribute concerned`) (h's `the basis of what was done`)
    WHEN JUST onBasis THEN
        IF onBasis AND h's `I was treated unfavourably` AND h's `the attribute was a substantial reason`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF h's `I was treated unfavourably` AND h's `the attribute was a substantial reason`
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 9(1): "Indirect discrimination occurs if a person imposes, or proposes to impose, a requirement, condition or practice
-- -- (a) that has, or is likely to have, the effect of disadvantaging persons with an attribute; and (b) that is not
-- reasonable." (2): the person who imposes it "has the burden of proving that [it] is reasonable".
GIVEN h IS A `What happened`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9 -- indirect discrimination` h MEANS
    IF h's `the attribute concerned` EQUALS `none of these attributes`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF h's `a requirement was imposed`
            AND h's `the requirement disadvantages people with the attribute`
            AND (NOT (h's `the requirement was proved reasonable`))
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 7(1)(a) with s 12(2): "A person does not discriminate against another person by taking a special measure."
GIVEN h IS A `What happened`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 7 to 12 -- I was discriminated against` h MEANS
    IF h's `it was proved to be a special measure`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE `either answer of` (`s 8 -- direct discrimination` h) `and` (`s 9 -- indirect discrimination` h)

-- s 12(3): "A special measure must -- (a) be undertaken in good faith ...; (b) be reasonably likely to achieve the
-- purpose ...; (c) be a proportionate means ...; (d) be justified because the members of the group have a particular need
-- for advancement or assistance." (6): burden on the person who undertakes it. (7): "On achieving the purpose ..., the
-- measure ceases to be a special measure."
GIVEN `in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reasonably likely to achieve it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `proportionate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `justified by a particular need` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose has been achieved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12 -- the measure is a special measure` `in good faith` `reasonably likely to achieve it` `proportionate` `justified by a particular need` `the purpose has been achieved` MEANS
    IF `the purpose has been achieved`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `in good faith` AND `reasonably likely to achieve it` AND `proportionate` AND `justified by a particular need`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Part 3 -- the positive duty (s 15) and investigations (s 127)`

-- s 15(1): "This section applies to a person who has a duty under Part 4, 6 or 7 not to engage in discrimination, sexual
-- harassment or victimisation." (2): "must take reasonable and proportionate measures to eliminate [it] as far as
-- possible." Every employer, principal, firm, industrial organisation and qualifying body has a Part 4 duty.
GIVEN `they have a duty under Part 4, 6 or 7` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15 -- the positive duty binds them` `they have a duty under Part 4, 6 or 7` MEANS
    IF `they have a duty under Part 4, 6 or 7`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- *limited by its own wording*: s 15 says only to whom it applies

-- s 127: "The Commission may conduct an investigation ... if -- (a) the matter -- (i) raises an issue that is serious in
-- nature; and (ii) relates to a class or group of persons; and (iii) cannot reasonably be expected to be resolved by dispute
-- resolution or by making an application to the Tribunal under section 122; and (b) there are reasonable grounds to
-- suspect that one or more contraventions of this Act have occurred; and (c) the investigation would advance the
-- objectives of this Act." s 15(4): a contravention of the positive duty "may be the subject of an investigation".
GIVEN `serious` IS A BOOLEAN
      `relates to a class or group` IS A BOOLEAN
      `cannot be resolved by dispute resolution or VCAT` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reasonable grounds to suspect a contravention` IS A BOOLEAN
      `would advance the objectives` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 127 -- the Commission may investigate` `serious` `relates to a class or group` `cannot be resolved by dispute resolution or VCAT` `reasonable grounds to suspect a contravention` `would advance the objectives` MEANS
    IF `serious` AND `relates to a class or group` AND `cannot be resolved by dispute resolution or VCAT` AND `reasonable grounds to suspect a contravention` AND `would advance the objectives`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Part 4 Divisions 1 and 2 -- discrimination at work (ss 16 to 37)`

-- The person's position: who the duty is owed to, and by whom.
DECLARE `Work position` IS ONE OF
    `a job applicant`                                      -- s 16 (employer)
    `a person offered employment`                          -- ss 16, 17, 20 (employer)
    `an employee`                                          -- ss 18, 19, 20 (employer)
    `a contract worker`                                    -- ss 21, 22, 22A (principal)
    `a person invited to join a firm being established`    -- ss 30, 33 (the person establishing it)
    `a person invited or seeking to become a partner`      -- ss 31(1), 32, 33 (firm)
    `a partner in a firm`                                  -- ss 31(2), 32, 33 (firm)
    `a person seeking to join an industrial organisation`  -- s 35(1) (the organisation and its governing body)
    `a member of an industrial organisation`               -- s 35(2)
    `a person dealing with a qualifying body`              -- s 36 (the body and each member)

DECLARE `What was done to me` IS ONE OF
    `deciding who should be offered the job, partnership or membership`
    `the terms offered to me`
    `refusing or failing to give me the job, membership or qualification`
    `denying me a guidance, apprenticeship or training program`
    `denying or limiting promotion, transfer, training or other benefits`
    `dismissing or expelling me, or taking away my membership or qualification`
    `not allowing me to work or continue to work`
    `the terms on which I am allowed to work`
    `varying the terms of my membership or qualification`
    `some other detriment`

-- ss 16, 18, 21(1), 30(1), 31(1), (2), 35(1), (2), 36(1): the heads each section lists for each position.
GIVEN `my position` IS A `Work position`, `what was done` IS A `What was done to me`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Part 4 Divisions 1 and 2 -- the section reaches what was done` `my position` `what was done` IF
    CONSIDER `my position`
    WHEN `a job applicant` THEN `the employer's offering heads` `what was done`
    WHEN `a person offered employment` THEN `the employer's offering heads` `what was done`
    WHEN `an employee` THEN
            `what was done` EQUALS `denying or limiting promotion, transfer, training or other benefits`
        OR  `what was done` EQUALS `dismissing or expelling me, or taking away my membership or qualification`
        OR  `what was done` EQUALS `denying me a guidance, apprenticeship or training program`
        OR  `what was done` EQUALS `some other detriment`
    WHEN `a contract worker` THEN
            `what was done` EQUALS `the terms on which I am allowed to work`
        OR  `what was done` EQUALS `not allowing me to work or continue to work`
        OR  `what was done` EQUALS `denying or limiting promotion, transfer, training or other benefits`
        OR  `what was done` EQUALS `some other detriment`
    WHEN `a person invited to join a firm being established` THEN
            `what was done` EQUALS `the terms offered to me`
    WHEN `a person invited or seeking to become a partner` THEN
            `what was done` EQUALS `deciding who should be offered the job, partnership or membership`
        OR  `what was done` EQUALS `the terms offered to me`
    WHEN `a partner in a firm` THEN
            `what was done` EQUALS `denying or limiting promotion, transfer, training or other benefits`
        OR  `what was done` EQUALS `dismissing or expelling me, or taking away my membership or qualification`
        OR  `what was done` EQUALS `some other detriment`
    WHEN `a person seeking to join an industrial organisation` THEN
            `what was done` EQUALS `deciding who should be offered the job, partnership or membership`
        OR  `what was done` EQUALS `refusing or failing to give me the job, membership or qualification`
        OR  `what was done` EQUALS `the terms offered to me`
    WHEN `a member of an industrial organisation` THEN
            `what was done` EQUALS `denying or limiting promotion, transfer, training or other benefits`
        OR  `what was done` EQUALS `dismissing or expelling me, or taking away my membership or qualification`
        OR  `what was done` EQUALS `varying the terms of my membership or qualification`
        OR  `what was done` EQUALS `some other detriment`
    WHEN `a person dealing with a qualifying body` THEN
            `what was done` EQUALS `refusing or failing to give me the job, membership or qualification`
        OR  `what was done` EQUALS `the terms offered to me`
        OR  `what was done` EQUALS `varying the terms of my membership or qualification`
        OR  `what was done` EQUALS `dismissing or expelling me, or taking away my membership or qualification`
        OR  `what was done` EQUALS `some other detriment`

-- s 16: "(a) in determining who should be offered employment; or (b) in the terms on which employment is offered ...; or
-- (c) by refusing or deliberately omitting to offer employment ...; or (d) by denying the person access to a guidance
-- program, an apprenticeship training program or other occupational training or retraining program."
GIVEN `what was done` IS A `What was done to me`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer's offering heads` `what was done` IF
        `what was done` EQUALS `deciding who should be offered the job, partnership or membership`
    OR  `what was done` EQUALS `the terms offered to me`
    OR  `what was done` EQUALS `refusing or failing to give me the job, membership or qualification`
    OR  `what was done` EQUALS `denying me a guidance, apprenticeship or training program`

GIVEN `my position` IS A `Work position`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the position is in a firm` `my position` IF
        `my position` EQUALS `a person invited to join a firm being established`
    OR  `my position` EQUALS `a person invited or seeking to become a partner`
    OR  `my position` EQUALS `a partner in a firm`

-- Part 4 Divisions 1 and 2 with s 13: "This Act does not prohibit discrimination to which a Division of Part 4 applies if
-- -- (a) an exception in that Division applies; or (b) ... an exception in the other Division applies; or (c) a general
-- exception under Part 5 applies; or (d) an exemption under Part 5 applies." (2): the exception is "a defence", and the
-- person relying on it "has the burden of proving that it applies".
-- s 21(2): s 21(1) "does not apply to anything done ... by a principal ... that would not contravene this Act if done ... by
-- the employer of that contract worker."
-- ss 30(2), 31(3), (4): a firm, or a firm being established, of "less than 5 partners may discriminate ... if the
-- discrimination is reasonable" (fork F2: unreasonable discrimination by a small firm, NOTHING).
GIVEN `my position`                     IS A `Work position`
      `what was done`                   IS A `What was done to me`
      `the firm has 5 or more partners` IS A BOOLEAN
      `was I discriminated against`     IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the small firm acted reasonably` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it would be lawful for my employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an exception or exemption is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Part 4 Divisions 1 and 2 -- the discrimination is prohibited` `my position` `what was done` `the firm has 5 or more partners` `was I discriminated against` `the small firm acted reasonably` `it would be lawful for my employer` `an exception or exemption is proved` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Part 4 Divisions 1 and 2 -- the section reaches what was done` `my position` `what was done`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- *limited by its own wording*: the section's list of heads for this position does not reach it
    ELSE CONSIDER `was I discriminated against`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
         WHEN JUST discriminated THEN
            IF NOT discriminated
            THEN JUST FALSE
            ELSE IF `my position` EQUALS `a contract worker` AND `it would be lawful for my employer`
                 THEN JUST FALSE
                 ELSE IF `the position is in a firm` `my position` AND (NOT `the firm has 5 or more partners`)
                      THEN IF `the small firm acted reasonably`
                           THEN JUST FALSE
                           ELSE NOTHING   -- *silent*: s 30(2), 31(3), (4) permit reasonable discrimination only; no prohibition for a small firm (fork F2)
                      ELSE IF `an exception or exemption is proved`
                           THEN JUST FALSE
                           ELSE JUST TRUE

-- ss 17, 19, 22, 32: the employer, principal or firm (5 or more partners, s 32) "must not, in relation to the work
-- arrangements of [the person], unreasonably refuse to accommodate the responsibilities that the [person] has as a parent
-- or carer." Contravention is discrimination (s 7(1)(b)). "carer" (s 4): a person on whom another is wholly or
-- substantially dependent for ongoing care and attention, not on a commercial basis.
GIVEN `my position`                         IS A `Work position`
      `the firm has 5 or more partners`     IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have parent or carer responsibilities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the refusal was unreasonable`        IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 17, 19, 22, 32 -- the refusal to accommodate me is prohibited` `my position` `the firm has 5 or more partners` `I have parent or carer responsibilities` `the refusal was unreasonable` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the parent or carer duty reaches` `my position` `the firm has 5 or more partners`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- *limited by its own wording*: ss 17, 19, 22, 32 name these positions only (a job applicant not yet offered, a small firm, a union or qualifying body: none)
    ELSE IF NOT `I have parent or carer responsibilities`
         THEN NOTHING   -- *limited by its own wording*
         ELSE IF `the refusal was unreasonable`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING   -- *limited by its own wording*: only an unreasonable refusal is prohibited (fork F3)

GIVEN `my position` IS A `Work position`, `the firm has 5 or more partners` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the parent or carer duty reaches` `my position` `the firm has 5 or more partners` IF
        `my position` EQUALS `a person offered employment`
    OR  `my position` EQUALS `an employee`
    OR  `my position` EQUALS `a contract worker`
    OR  (   (   `my position` EQUALS `a person invited or seeking to become a partner`
             OR `my position` EQUALS `a partner in a firm`
             OR `my position` EQUALS `a person invited to join a firm being established`)
        AND `the firm has 5 or more partners`)

-- ss 20, 22A, 33: the section "applies to a person with a disability who ... requires adjustments in order to perform the
-- genuine and reasonable requirements of the employment [work, partnership]." (2): the employer, principal or firm "must
-- make reasonable adjustments unless the person ... could not or cannot adequately perform the genuine and reasonable
-- requirements ... even after the adjustments are made." (5): "not required to make an adjustment ... to the extent that
-- [it] has complied with, or has been exempted from compliance with, a relevant disability standard" (Disability
-- Discrimination Act 1992 (Cth)). (6): nor one relating to a building or land under a s 160B Building Act 1993
-- determination it complies with. Contravention of ss 20, 33 is discrimination (s 7(1)(b)); s 22A is not listed there
-- (finding 2).
GIVEN `my position`                         IS A `Work position`
      `I have a disability`                 IS A BOOLEAN
      `I need adjustments to do the work`   IS A BOOLEAN
      `I could do the work after the adjustments` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the adjustment is reasonable`        IS A BOOLEAN
      `a disability standard covers it and was complied with or exempted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a building determination covers it and is complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 20, 22A, 33 -- they must make the adjustment` `my position` `I have a disability` `I need adjustments to do the work` `I could do the work after the adjustments` `the adjustment is reasonable` `a disability standard covers it and was complied with or exempted` `a building determination covers it and is complied with` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the adjustment duty reaches` `my position`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- *limited by its own wording*
    ELSE IF NOT (`I have a disability` AND `I need adjustments to do the work`)
         THEN NOTHING   -- *limited by its own wording*: "This section applies to ..."
         ELSE IF NOT `I could do the work after the adjustments`
              THEN JUST FALSE   -- "unless"
              ELSE IF `a disability standard covers it and was complied with or exempted` OR `a building determination covers it and is complied with`
                   THEN JUST FALSE   -- "is not required"
                   ELSE IF `the adjustment is reasonable`
                        THEN JUST TRUE
                        ELSE NOTHING   -- *limited by its own wording*: the duty is to make reasonable adjustments (fork F4)

GIVEN `my position` IS A `Work position`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the adjustment duty reaches` `my position` IF
        `my position` EQUALS `a person offered employment`
    OR  `my position` EQUALS `an employee`
    OR  `my position` EQUALS `a contract worker`
    OR  `the position is in a firm` `my position`

§§ `The exceptions in Divisions 1 and 2 (ss 23 to 29, 34, 37)`

GIVEN `my position` IS A `Work position`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the position is in sections 16 or 18` `my position` IF
        `my position` EQUALS `a job applicant`
    OR  `my position` EQUALS `a person offered employment`
    OR  `my position` EQUALS `an employee`

GIVEN `my position` IS A `Work position`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the position is an offer of employment` `my position` IF
        `my position` EQUALS `a job applicant`
    OR  `my position` EQUALS `a person offered employment`

-- s 23: "An employer may discriminate against a person or an employee on the basis of the person's or employee's
-- disability in any of the areas specified in section 16 or 18 if -- (a) the person or employee requires adjustments ...;
-- and (b) in the case of a person to whom section 20 applies, the employer has complied with that section; and (c) in any
-- case, either -- (i) the adjustments are not reasonable adjustments ...; or (ii) the person or employee could not or
-- cannot adequately perform the genuine and reasonable requirements ... even after the adjustments are made".
-- s 34: the same for a firm, but (b) reads "in the case of a person to whom section 32 applies, the firm has complied with
-- that section" -- s 32 is the parent or carer duty, not the adjustment duty (s 33): finding 3, encoded as printed.
GIVEN `my position`                         IS A `Work position`
      `the attribute`                       IS AN `Attribute`
      `I need adjustments to do the work`   IS A BOOLEAN
      `they complied with the section paragraph (b) names` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the firm has 5 or more partners`     IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have parent or carer responsibilities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the adjustments are not reasonable`  IS A BOOLEAN
      `I could not do the work even after the adjustments` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 23, 34 -- the disability exception applies` `my position` `the attribute` `I need adjustments to do the work` `they complied with the section paragraph (b) names` `the firm has 5 or more partners` `I have parent or carer responsibilities` `the adjustments are not reasonable` `I could not do the work even after the adjustments` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the position is in sections 16 or 18` `my position` OR `the position is in a firm` `my position`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- *limited by its own wording*: ss 23, 34 cover the areas of ss 16, 18, 30, 31 only
    ELSE IF NOT (`the attribute` EQUALS `disability`)
         THEN NOTHING   -- *limited by its own wording*: the exception is for disability only
         ELSE IF `I need adjustments to do the work` AND `paragraph (b) is met` AND (`the adjustments are not reasonable` OR `I could not do the work even after the adjustments`)
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `the section (b) names applies` MEANS
            IF `the position is in a firm` `my position`
            THEN `the firm has 5 or more partners` AND `I have parent or carer responsibilities` AND (NOT (`my position` EQUALS `a person invited to join a firm being established`))
            ELSE (`my position` EQUALS `a person offered employment` OR `my position` EQUALS `an employee`) AND `I need adjustments to do the work`
        `paragraph (b) is met` MEANS
            IF `the section (b) names applies`
            THEN `they complied with the section paragraph (b) names`
            ELSE TRUE

-- s 24(1): "An employer may discriminate in determining who should be offered employment in relation to the provision
-- of domestic or personal services (including the care, instruction or supervision of children) -- (a) in the
-- employer's home; or (b) if the employer is in the business of providing domestic or personal services to others, in the
-- home of the person to whom those services are provided if the discrimination is requested by or on behalf of that
-- person."
DECLARE `Where the domestic services are given` IS ONE OF
    `in the employer's own home`
    `in a client's home, at the client's request`
    `in a client's home, without the client's request`
    `elsewhere`

GIVEN `my position`         IS A `Work position`
      `what was done`       IS A `What was done to me`
      `the job is domestic or personal services` IS A BOOLEAN
      `where`               IS A `Where the domestic services are given`
      `the employer is in the business of providing them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 24 -- the domestic services exception applies` `my position` `what was done` `the job is domestic or personal services` `where` `the employer is in the business of providing them` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the position is an offer of employment` `my position` AND `what was done` EQUALS `deciding who should be offered the job, partnership or membership`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- *limited by its own wording*: "in determining who should be offered employment"
    ELSE IF `the job is domestic or personal services`
            AND (   `where` EQUALS `in the employer's own home`
                 OR (`where` EQUALS `in a client's home, at the client's request` AND `the employer is in the business of providing them`))
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 25(1): "Nothing in section 16 or 18 applies to discrimination by an employer against a person or employee if -- (a) the
-- employment involves the care, instruction or supervision of children; and (b) the discrimination is reasonably
-- necessary to protect the physical, psychological or emotional wellbeing of the children." (2): not employment by a
-- post-secondary education provider.
GIVEN `my position` IS A `Work position`
      `the job involves caring for, instructing or supervising children` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is reasonably necessary to protect the children` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer is a post-secondary education provider` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25 -- the care of children exception applies` `my position` `the job involves caring for, instructing or supervising children` `it is reasonably necessary to protect the children` `the employer is a post-secondary education provider` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the position is in sections 16 or 18` `my position`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- *limited by its own wording*
    ELSE IF `the employer is a post-secondary education provider`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- s 25(2) "does not apply"
         ELSE IF `the job involves caring for, instructing or supervising children` AND `it is reasonably necessary to protect the children`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 26(1), (2): limiting employment to one sex where it is a genuine occupational requirement; (2) lists cases that are
-- one "without limiting the generality of subsection (1)".
DECLARE `Why one sex is required` IS ONE OF
    `physical characteristics only that sex has, other than strength or stamina`   -- (2)(a)
    `fitting clothing for that sex, for decency or privacy`                        -- (2)(b)
    `searching the clothing or bodies of that sex`                                 -- (2)(c)
    `entering a lavatory in use by that sex`                                       -- (2)(d)
    `entering areas used only by that sex while they are undressed`                -- (2)(e)
    `another genuine occupational requirement`                                     -- (1), a judgment
    `no genuine occupational requirement`

-- s 26(3): "An employer may limit the offering of employment in relation to a dramatic or an artistic performance,
-- entertainment, photographic or modelling work or any other employment -- (a) to people of a particular age, sex or race;
-- (b) to people with or without a particular disability -- if it is necessary to do so for reasons of authenticity or
-- credibility." (4): "may discriminate on the basis of physical features in the offering of employment in relation to a
-- dramatic or an artistic performance, photographic or modelling work or any similar employment." (5): profession, trade or
-- occupation, "if experience in a particular profession, trade or occupation is relevant to the employment or offer and is
-- a genuine occupational requirement for the position or role on offer and it is reasonable to discriminate on that
-- basis in the circumstances."
GIVEN `my position`         IS A `Work position`
      `what was done`       IS A `What was done to me`
      `the attribute`       IS AN `Attribute`
      `why one sex`         IS A `Why one sex is required`
      `necessary for authenticity or credibility` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the job is a performance, photographic, modelling or similar work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the experience is relevant, a genuine requirement and reasonable to insist on` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 26 -- a genuine occupational requirement exception applies` `my position` `what was done` `the attribute` `why one sex` `necessary for authenticity or credibility` `the job is a performance, photographic, modelling or similar work` `the experience is relevant, a genuine requirement and reasonable to insist on` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the position is an offer of employment` `my position` AND `the employer's offering heads` `what was done` AND (NOT (`what was done` EQUALS `denying me a guidance, apprenticeship or training program`)))
    THEN NOTHING   -- *limited by its own wording*: "the offering of employment"
    ELSE IF `the attribute` EQUALS `sex`
         THEN IF (NOT (`why one sex` EQUALS `no genuine occupational requirement`)) OR `necessary for authenticity or credibility`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF `the attribute` EQUALS `age` OR `the attribute` EQUALS `race` OR `the attribute` EQUALS `disability`
              THEN IF `necessary for authenticity or credibility`
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE JUST FALSE
              ELSE IF `the attribute` EQUALS `physical features`
                   THEN IF `the job is a performance, photographic, modelling or similar work`
                        THEN JUST TRUE
                        ELSE JUST FALSE
                   ELSE IF `the attribute` EQUALS `profession trade or occupation`
                        THEN IF `the experience is relevant, a genuine requirement and reasonable to insist on`
                             THEN JUST TRUE
                             ELSE JUST FALSE
                        ELSE NOTHING   -- *limited by its own wording*: s 26 names sex, age, race, disability, physical features, profession

-- s 27: "An employer may discriminate on the basis of political belief or activity in the offering of employment to
-- another person as a ministerial adviser, member of staff of a political party, member of the electorate staff of any
-- person or any similar employment."
GIVEN `my position` IS A `Work position`
      `the attribute` IS AN `Attribute`
      `the job is political staff work` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27 -- the political employment exception applies` `my position` `the attribute` `the job is political staff work` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the position is an offer of employment` `my position`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- *limited by its own wording*
    ELSE IF NOT (`the attribute` EQUALS `political belief or activity`)
         THEN NOTHING   -- *limited by its own wording*
         ELSE IF `the job is political staff work`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING   -- *limited by its own wording*: a permission with no "only"

-- s 28: "An employer may limit the offering of employment to people with a particular attribute in relation to the
-- provision of services for people with the same attribute if those services -- (a) are either -- (i) a special measure
-- under section 12; or (ii) a service for special needs under section 88; and (b) can be provided most effectively by
-- people with that attribute."
GIVEN `my position` IS A `Work position`
      `the services are for people with the attribute` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are a special measure or a special needs service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `people with the attribute provide them most effectively` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28 -- the welfare services exception applies` `my position` `the services are for people with the attribute` `they are a special measure or a special needs service` `people with the attribute provide them most effectively` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the position is an offer of employment` `my position`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- *limited by its own wording*
    ELSE IF NOT `the services are for people with the attribute`
         THEN NOTHING   -- *limited by its own wording*
         ELSE IF `they are a special measure or a special needs service` AND `people with the attribute provide them most effectively`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 28A: "An employer may pay an employee who is under the age of 21 years according to the employee's age."
GIVEN `my position` IS A `Work position`, `my age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28A -- I may be paid a youth wage` `my position` `my age` MEANS
    IF NOT (`my position` EQUALS `an employee`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- *limited by its own wording*
    ELSE IF `my age` LESS THAN 21
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- *limited by its own wording*: a scope limit with no "only" (ruling (c) of 2026-11-05)

-- s 29: "In deciding the terms on which to offer an employee an incentive to resign or retire, an employer may take into
-- account the age of the employee and any eligibility of the employee to receive a retirement benefit from a
-- superannuation fund."
GIVEN `my position` IS A `Work position`, `it is an offer of an incentive to resign or retire` IS A BOOLEAN, `the attribute` IS AN `Attribute`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29 -- the early retirement exception applies` `my position` `it is an offer of an incentive to resign or retire` `the attribute` MEANS
    IF (`my position` EQUALS `an employee`) AND `it is an offer of an incentive to resign or retire` AND `the attribute` EQUALS `age`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- *limited by its own wording*

-- s 37: "A qualifying body may set reasonable terms in relation to an occupational qualification, or make reasonable
-- variations to those terms, to enable a person with a disability to practise ..."
GIVEN `my position` IS A `Work position`, `the attribute` IS AN `Attribute`, `the terms are reasonable and enable me to practise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 37 -- the qualification terms exception applies` `my position` `the attribute` `the terms are reasonable and enable me to practise` MEANS
    IF `my position` EQUALS `a person dealing with a qualifying body` AND `the attribute` EQUALS `disability` AND `the terms are reasonable and enable me to practise`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- *limited by its own wording*

§§ `Part 5 -- the general exceptions an employer can rely on (ss 75, 76, 82A, 83A, 86)`

-- s 75(1): "A person may discriminate if the discrimination is necessary to comply with, or is authorised by, a provision
-- of -- (a) an Act, other than this Act; or (b) an enactment, other than an enactment under this Act." s 76: "necessary to
-- comply with -- (a) an order of the Tribunal; or (b) an order of any other tribunal or any court."
GIVEN `required or authorised by another law` IS A BOOLEAN, `necessary to comply with a court or tribunal order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 75, 76 -- the statutory authority or court order exception applies` `required or authorised by another law` `necessary to comply with a court or tribunal order` MEANS
    IF `required or authorised by another law` OR `necessary to comply with a court or tribunal order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 82A(1) (religious body) and s 83A(1) (religious school): "A person may discriminate against another person in
-- relation to the employment of the other person in a particular position ... if -- (a) conformity with the doctrines,
-- beliefs or principles of the ... religion is an inherent requirement of the position; and (b) the other person cannot
-- meet that inherent requirement because of their religious belief or activity; and (c) the discrimination is reasonable
-- and proportionate in the circumstances." (3): "does not permit discrimination on the basis of any attribute other than
-- as specified in subsection (1)."
GIVEN `the employer is a religious body or religious school` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the attribute` IS AN `Attribute`
      `conformity is an inherent requirement of the position` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I cannot meet it because of my religious belief or activity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reasonable and proportionate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 82A, 83A -- the religious employer exception applies` `the employer is a religious body or religious school` `the attribute` `conformity is an inherent requirement of the position` `I cannot meet it because of my religious belief or activity` `reasonable and proportionate` MEANS
    IF NOT `the employer is a religious body or religious school`
    THEN NOTHING   -- *limited by its own wording*
    ELSE IF NOT (`the attribute` EQUALS `religious belief or activity`)
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- (3) "does not permit discrimination on the basis of any attribute other than ..."
         ELSE IF `conformity is an inherent requirement of the position` AND `I cannot meet it because of my religious belief or activity` AND `reasonable and proportionate`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 86(1): "A person may discriminate against another person on the basis of disability or physical features if the
-- discrimination is reasonably necessary -- (a) to protect the health or safety of any person (including the person
-- discriminated against) or of the public generally; or (b) to protect the property of any person ... or any public
-- property." (2): "on the basis of pregnancy if the discrimination is reasonably necessary to protect the health or safety
-- of any person".
GIVEN `the attribute` IS AN `Attribute`
      `reasonably necessary for health or safety` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reasonably necessary to protect property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 86 -- the health, safety and property exception applies` `the attribute` `reasonably necessary for health or safety` `reasonably necessary to protect property` MEANS
    IF `the attribute` EQUALS `disability` OR `the attribute` EQUALS `physical features`
    THEN IF `reasonably necessary for health or safety` OR `reasonably necessary to protect property`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the attribute` EQUALS `pregnancy`
         THEN IF `reasonably necessary for health or safety`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- *limited by its own wording*: s 86 names disability, physical features and pregnancy

§§ `Part 6 -- sexual harassment (ss 92 to 102)`

DECLARE `Kind of conduct` IS ONE OF
    `an unwelcome sexual advance`
    `an unwelcome request for sexual favours`
    `other unwelcome conduct of a sexual nature`   -- s 92(2): physical intimacy, remarks with sexual connotations, sexual gestures, actions or comments
    `conduct that was welcome or not sexual`

-- s 92(1): "a person sexually harasses another person if he or she -- (a) makes an unwelcome sexual advance, or an
-- unwelcome request for sexual favours, to the other person; or (b) engages in any other unwelcome conduct of a sexual
-- nature in relation to the other person -- in circumstances in which a reasonable person, having regard to all the
-- circumstances, would have anticipated that the other person would be offended, humiliated or intimidated."
GIVEN `the conduct` IS A `Kind of conduct`, `a reasonable person would have anticipated offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 92 -- it was sexual harassment` `the conduct` `a reasonable person would have anticipated offence` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`the conduct` EQUALS `conduct that was welcome or not sexual`)) AND `a reasonable person would have anticipated offence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- ss 93 to 102: who must not sexually harass whom. "employee", "employer" and "employment" include unpaid workers and
-- volunteers in Part 6 (s 4). s 93(3): a municipal councillor, and a member of the governing body of a body corporate or
-- unincorporated association, is taken to be the employer of its employees.
DECLARE `Who harassed me` IS ONE OF
    `my employer or the employer I was seeking work from`                         -- s 93(1)
    `a person employed by my employer or by the employer I was seeking work from` -- s 93(2)(a), (c)
    `a person I employ`                                                           -- s 93(2)(b)
    `a person at a place that is a workplace of both of us`                       -- s 94
    `a partner in the firm I am a partner in or am seeking to join`               -- s 95
    `a member or employee of an industrial organisation I belong to, work for or seek to join` -- s 96
    `a member or employee of a qualifying body I deal with, belong to or work for` -- s 97
    `a staff member or authority member of an educational institution where I study or seek to study` -- s 98(1), (3)
    `a student at an educational institution where I study, work or sit on the authority` -- s 98(2)
    `a person providing or offering goods or services to me, or receiving them from me` -- s 99
    `a person providing or offering accommodation to me`                          -- s 100
    `a member of a club I belong to, work for or seek to join`                    -- s 101
    `a councillor of the council I am a councillor or committee member of`        -- s 102
    `someone in none of these relationships with me`

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A `Kind of conduct`
      `a reasonable person would have anticipated offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `who` IS A `Who harassed me`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Part 6 -- the sexual harassment is prohibited` `the conduct` `a reasonable person would have anticipated offence` `who` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 92 -- it was sexual harassment` `the conduct` `a reasonable person would have anticipated offence`
    WHEN JUST harassed THEN
        IF NOT harassed
        THEN JUST FALSE
        ELSE IF `who` EQUALS `someone in none of these relationships with me`
             THEN NOTHING   -- *limited by its own wording*: ss 93 to 102 name the relationships and places
             ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

§§ `Part 7 -- victimisation, authorising or assisting, requests for information, vicarious liability (ss 103 to 110)`

-- s 104(1): "A person victimises another person if the person subjects or threatens to subject the other person to any
-- detriment because the other person, or a person associated with the other person -- (a) has brought a dispute to the
-- Commission ...; (b) has made a complaint ... under the old Act or the Racial and Religious Tolerance Act 2001; (c) has
-- brought any other proceedings ...; (d) has given evidence or information, or produced a document ...; (e) has attended
-- a compulsory conference or mediation at the Tribunal ...; (f) has otherwise done anything in accordance with this Act
-- ...; (g) has alleged that any person has contravened a provision of Part 4, 6 or 6A or this Part ... unless the
-- allegation is false and was not made in good faith; or (h) has refused to do anything that ... would contravene [them]
-- -- or because the person believes that the other person or the associate has done or intends to do any of those
-- things." (3)(a): the reason need not be the only or dominant one "provided that it is a substantial reason".
DECLARE `What I or my associate did` IS ONE OF
    `brought a dispute to the Commission`                                        -- (a)
    `made a complaint under the old Act or the Racial and Religious Tolerance Act` -- (b)
    `brought other proceedings under this Act or those Acts`                     -- (c)
    `gave evidence, information or a document in proceedings or a Commission investigation` -- (d)
    `attended a compulsory conference or mediation at VCAT`                      -- (e)
    `did anything else in accordance with this Act or those Acts`                -- (f)
    `alleged that someone contravened the Act`                                   -- (g)
    `refused to do something that would contravene the Act`                      -- (h)
    `none of these`

GIVEN `what was done or believed` IS A `What I or my associate did`
      `I was subjected or threatened with a detriment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was a substantial reason` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the allegation was false and not in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 104 -- I was victimised` `what was done or believed` `I was subjected or threatened with a detriment` `it was a substantial reason` `the allegation was false and not in good faith` MEANS
    IF `what was done or believed` EQUALS `none of these`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `what was done or believed` EQUALS `alleged that someone contravened the Act` AND `the allegation was false and not in good faith`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- (g) "unless"
         ELSE IF `I was subjected or threatened with a detriment` AND `it was a substantial reason`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 105: "A person must not request, instruct, induce, encourage, authorise or assist another person to contravene a
-- provision of Part 4, 6 or 6A or this Part." s 106: if, as a result, the other person contravenes, "a person may (a)
-- bring a dispute to the Commission ...; or (b) make an application to the Tribunal -- against either the person who
-- authorises or assists or the person who contravenes ... or both".
GIVEN `they requested, instructed, induced, encouraged, authorised or assisted it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other person contravened as a result` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 105, 106 -- I can bring my claim against the person who authorised or assisted` `they requested, instructed, induced, encouraged, authorised or assisted it` `the other person contravened as a result` MEANS
    IF `they requested, instructed, induced, encouraged, authorised or assisted it` AND `the other person contravened as a result`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `they requested, instructed, induced, encouraged, authorised or assisted it`
         THEN NOTHING   -- *silent*: s 105 is contravened, but s 106 gives the claim only where the contravention followed (fork F7)
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 107(1): "A person must not request or require another person to supply information that could be used by the first
-- person to form the basis of discrimination against the other person." s 108(1): may, "if the information is reasonably
-- required for a purpose that does not involve prohibited discrimination"; (2) burden on the requester.
GIVEN `the information could be used to discriminate against me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they proved it is reasonably required for a non-discriminatory purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 107, 108 -- the request for information is prohibited` `the information could be used to discriminate against me` `they proved it is reasonably required for a non-discriminatory purpose` MEANS
    IF NOT `the information could be used to discriminate against me`
    THEN NOTHING   -- *limited by its own wording*
    ELSE IF `they proved it is reasonably required for a non-discriminatory purpose`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- s 108(1) "may"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- s 108(3): the requester "(a) must not directly or indirectly disclose or communicate the information to any person
-- unless it is necessary to do so for the purpose ...; and (b) must destroy or permanently de-identify the information
-- when it is no longer required for the purpose".
GIVEN `it is still required for the purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 108(3)(b) -- they must destroy or de-identify my information` `it is still required for the purpose` MEANS
    IF `it is still required for the purpose`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- "when" counts as "where" (ruling (c) of 2026-11-05)
    ELSE JUST TRUE

GIVEN `it is necessary for the purpose to disclose it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 108(3)(a) -- they must not pass my information on` `it is necessary for the purpose to disclose it` MEANS
    IF `it is necessary for the purpose to disclose it`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- "unless" met (fork F8)
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- s 109: "If a person in the course of employment or while acting as an agent -- (a) contravenes a provision of Part 4, 6
-- or 6A or this Part; or (b) engages in any conduct that would, if engaged in by the person's employer or principal,
-- contravene [one] -- both the person and the employer or principal must be taken to have contravened the provision and
-- a person may bring a dispute ... or make an application to the Tribunal against either or both of them." s 110: "not
-- vicariously liable ... if the employer or principal proves, on the balance of probabilities, that [it] took reasonable
-- precautions to prevent the employee or agent contravening this Act."
GIVEN `they acted in the course of employment or as an agent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what they did contravenes, or would if the employer did it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer proved reasonable precautions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 109, 110 -- the employer or principal is liable too` `they acted in the course of employment or as an agent` `what they did contravenes, or would if the employer did it` `the employer proved reasonable precautions` MEANS
    IF NOT (`they acted in the course of employment or as an agent` AND `what they did contravenes, or would if the employer did it`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- "If"
    ELSE IF `the employer proved reasonable precautions`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- s 110 "is not vicariously liable ... if"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `Part 8 -- disputes and applications (ss 113 to 126)`

-- What the dispute is about.
DECLARE `What my claim is about` IS ONE OF
    `discrimination under Part 4`
    `sexual harassment under Part 6`
    `vilification under Part 6A`
    `victimisation or another contravention of Part 7`
    `only a breach of the positive duty in section 15`
    `only an offence such as discriminatory advertising`

-- ss 113(1), 123(1): "(a) a person who claims that another person has contravened a provision of Part 4, 6, 6A or 7 in
-- relation to that person; (b) if that person is unable to bring a dispute [make an application] because of disability
-- -- (i) a person authorised by that person to act on his or her behalf; or (ii) if that person is unable to authorise
-- another person, any other person on his or her behalf; (c) if that person is a child -- (i) the child; or (ii) a parent
-- of the child on the child's behalf; or (iii) if the Commission [Tribunal] is satisfied that the child or a parent of
-- the child consents, any other person on the child's behalf."
DECLARE `Who is bringing it` IS ONE OF
    `I am, about a contravention in relation to me`
    `a person I authorised, because my disability prevents me`
    `any person for me, because my disability prevents me from authorising anyone`
    `my parent, because I am a child`
    `another person for me as a child, with consent the Commission or VCAT accepts`
    `another person for me as a child, without that consent`
    `another person for me, in none of these ways`

GIVEN `who brings it` IS A `Who is bringing it`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 113(1), 123(1) -- the person bringing it may do so` `who brings it` MEANS
    IF `who brings it` EQUALS `another person for me as a child, without that consent`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- (c)(iii) "if the Commission [Tribunal] is satisfied"
    ELSE IF `who brings it` EQUALS `another person for me, in none of these ways`
         THEN NOTHING   -- *limited by its own wording*: the list is not closed with "only" (representative bodies: ss 114, 124)
         ELSE JUST TRUE

GIVEN `about` IS A `What my claim is about`, `who brings it` IS A `Who is bringing it`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 113, 122, 123 -- the dispute or application can be brought` `about` `who brings it` MEANS
    IF `about` EQUALS `only a breach of the positive duty in section 15`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- s 15(3) "Part 8 does not apply"
    ELSE IF `about` EQUALS `only an offence such as discriminatory advertising`
         THEN NOTHING   -- *limited by its own wording*: Part 8 covers Parts 4, 6, 6A, 7; offences are prosecuted under Part 12
         ELSE `ss 113(1), 123(1) -- the person bringing it may do so` `who brings it`

-- s 116: "The Commission may decline to provide or to continue to provide dispute resolution for any of the following
-- reasons -- (a) the alleged contravention occurred more than 12 months before the dispute was brought; (b) the matter has
-- been adequately dealt with by a court or tribunal; (c) the matter involves subject matter that would be more
-- appropriately dealt with by a court or tribunal; (d) a person has initiated proceedings in another forum; (e) having
-- regard to all the circumstances, the Commission considers it is not appropriate ..."
GIVEN `the day of the contravention` IS A DATE, `the day the dispute was brought` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 116(a) -- the contravention was more than 12 months before the dispute` `the day of the contravention` `the day the dispute was brought` MEANS
    IF `the day of the contravention` `is before` (`the date` 12 `months before` `the day the dispute was brought`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- a period the text fixes (ruling (a) of 2026-11-05)

GIVEN `the day of the contravention` IS A DATE
      `the day the dispute was brought` IS A DATE
      `adequately dealt with by a court or tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `more appropriately dealt with by a court or tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `proceedings started in another forum` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission considers it not appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 116 -- the Commission may decline my dispute` `the day of the contravention` `the day the dispute was brought` `adequately dealt with by a court or tribunal` `more appropriately dealt with by a court or tribunal` `proceedings started in another forum` `the Commission considers it not appropriate` MEANS
    IF `the answer` (`s 116(a) -- the contravention was more than 12 months before the dispute` `the day of the contravention` `the day the dispute was brought`) `is yes`
        OR `adequately dealt with by a court or tribunal`
        OR `more appropriately dealt with by a court or tribunal`
        OR `proceedings started in another forum`
        OR `the Commission considers it not appropriate`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- "for any of the following reasons", read as closed (fork F10)

-- s 115(1): "Dispute resolution starts when the person bringing the dispute informs the Commission that he or she wishes
-- to proceed". (2): "ends when the earliest of the following occurs -- (a) the Commission declines ... under section 116;
-- (b) a party withdraws ... under section 118; (c) the parties to the dispute reach agreement about the subject matter".
GIVEN `I told the Commission I wish to proceed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission declined` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a party withdrew` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the parties reached agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 115 -- dispute resolution has ended` `I told the Commission I wish to proceed` `the Commission declined` `a party withdrew` `the parties reached agreement` MEANS
    IF NOT `I told the Commission I wish to proceed`
    THEN NOTHING   -- *silent*: s 115(2) speaks of a dispute resolution that has started
    ELSE IF `the Commission declined` OR `a party withdrew` OR `the parties reached agreement`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 117(1): "Evidence of anything said or done in the course of dispute resolution is inadmissible in proceedings before
-- the Tribunal or any other legal proceeding relating to the subject matter of the dispute."
GIVEN `it was said or done in dispute resolution` IS A BOOLEAN, `the proceeding relates to the subject matter of the dispute` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117 -- it can be used as evidence` `it was said or done in dispute resolution` `the proceeding relates to the subject matter of the dispute` MEANS
    IF `it was said or done in dispute resolution` AND `the proceeding relates to the subject matter of the dispute`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- *points outside the text*: admissibility is then for the law of evidence

-- s 119(3): "A request [for a written record of agreement] must be made within 30 days after the agreement is reached."
DECLARE `Party to the agreement` IS ONE OF `the party who asks for the record`
DECLARE `Record request` IS ONE OF `request a written record of the agreement`

GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party to the agreement` `Record request`
`s 119(3) -- the request for a record must be made within 30 days` MEANS
    PARTY `the party who asks for the record`
    MUST `request a written record of the agreement`
    WITHIN 30
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the party who asks for the record` BECAUSE "the request for a written record of agreement was not made within 30 days after the agreement was reached (s 119(3)); the agreement stays valid (s 119(7)) but no record is prepared under s 119"

DECLARE `What became of the request` IS ONE OF
    `made in time`
    `made too late`
    `still open`
    `made before the agreement was reached`

-- The helper that runs the duty over what happened (in the shape of the Civil Procedure Act 2010 encoding's). On the
-- stable l4 a CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE can match FULFILLED but not BREACH. It takes a DEONTIC value, so it is never
-- exported.
GIVEN `the rule`              IS A DEONTIC `Party to the agreement` `Record request`
      `the request was made`  IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time of the request` IS A NUMBER
      `the time now`          IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `What became of the request`
`what became of the record request` `the rule` `the request was made` `the time of the request` `the time now` MEANS
    IF `the request was made`
    THEN CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time of the request`), (EVENT `the party who asks for the record` `request a written record of the agreement` `the time of the request`))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `made in time`
         OTHERWISE `made too late`
    ELSE CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time now`), (EVENT `the party who asks for the record` `request a written record of the agreement` `the time now`))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `still open`
         OTHERWISE `made too late`

GIVEN `the day the agreement was reached` IS A DATE
      `I have made the request`           IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the request`            IS A DATE
      `today`                             IS A DATE
GIVETH A `What became of the request`
`s 119(3) -- what became of my request for a record` `the day the agreement was reached` `I have made the request` `the day of the request` `today` MEANS
    IF `I have made the request` AND `the day of the request` `is before` `the day the agreement was reached`
    THEN `made before the agreement was reached`
    ELSE `what became of the record request` `s 119(3) -- the request for a record must be made within 30 days` `I have made the request` (`the days from` `the day the agreement was reached` `to` `the day of the request`) (`the days from` `the day the agreement was reached` `to` `today`)

-- s 120(1): "Any party, after notifying the other party in writing, may lodge a copy of the signed and certified record of
-- agreement with the Tribunal for registration." (2): "Subject to subsection (3), the Tribunal must register the
-- agreement". (3): it may refuse if it "considers that it may not be practicable to enforce, or to supervise compliance
-- with" it. (4): on registration it "must be taken to be an order of the Tribunal ... and may be enforced accordingly".
GIVEN `the record is signed by each party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission certified the record` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I notified the other party in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `VCAT considers it may not be practicable to enforce` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 120 -- VCAT must register my agreement` `the record is signed by each party` `the Commission certified the record` `I notified the other party in writing` `VCAT considers it may not be practicable to enforce` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the record is signed by each party` AND `the Commission certified the record` AND `I notified the other party in writing`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- (1): only a signed and certified record, after written notice (fork F11)
    ELSE IF `VCAT considers it may not be practicable to enforce`
         THEN NOTHING   -- *limited by its own wording*: VCAT "may refuse"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- s 121(2), (3): the person bringing the dispute may apply for an interim order; "An application may be made at any time
-- before an application under section 122 relating to the dispute has been made to the Tribunal." (5): the order lasts
-- "not exceeding 28 days", and may be extended.
GIVEN `I brought the dispute to the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN, `I have applied to VCAT under section 122` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121 -- I may apply for an interim order` `I brought the dispute to the Commission` `I have applied to VCAT under section 122` MEANS
    IF NOT `I brought the dispute to the Commission`
    THEN NOTHING   -- *limited by its own wording*: s 121(2) names the person bringing the dispute and the Commission
    ELSE IF `I have applied to VCAT under section 122`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- a period the text fixes ("before")
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- s 125: after hearing, VCAT may "(a) find that a person has contravened a provision of Part 4, 6, 6A or 7 and make ...
-- (i) an order that the person refrain from committing any further contravention ...; (ii) an order that the person pay to
-- the applicant, within a specified period, an amount the Tribunal thinks fit to compensate the applicant for loss, damage
-- or injury suffered in consequence of the contravention; (iii) an order that the person do anything specified ... with a
-- view to redressing any loss, damage or injury ...; or (b) find [a contravention] but decline to take any further action;
-- or (c) find that a person has not contravened ... and make an order that the application ... be dismissed."
GIVEN `VCAT found a contravention` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 125 -- VCAT may order compensation` `VCAT found a contravention` MEANS
    IF `VCAT found a contravention`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 126: "(1) This section applies if -- (a) the Tribunal has made an order referred to in section 125(a); and (b) a
-- person has failed to comply with the order. (2) If the applicant consents, the Commission may enforce the order on
-- behalf of the applicant".
GIVEN `VCAT made an order under section 125(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has not complied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I consent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 126 -- the Commission may enforce my order` `VCAT made an order under section 125(a)` `the person has not complied` `I consent` MEANS
    IF `VCAT made an order under section 125(a)` AND `the person has not complied` AND `I consent`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
